---
/**
 * The reader-initiated next step. Governance rules:
 * - clearly labeled as a service pathway, visually separate from editorial
 * - educational framing, explicit no-obligation, relationship disclosure linked
 * - never urgency language, never on governance pages
 */
---
<aside class="assessment-note" aria-labelledby="assessment-heading">
  <p class="assessment-note__label">A practical next step · <a href="/about/how-cri-works/">how CRI works</a></p>
  <h2 id="assessment-heading">Want eyes on your actual roof?</h2>
  <p>
    Reading is planning-grade; decisions need building-specific facts. CRI can arrange a
    <strong>complimentary commercial roof assessment</strong> — a documented walk-through
    with photos and a written condition summary you keep, whatever you decide to do next.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>No obligation, and no follow-up sales pressure — that's a condition of our <a href="/about/funding-and-relationships/">partner relationships</a>.</li>
    <li>Performed by a <a href="/about/how-cri-works/#partner-standards">vetted</a> commercial roofing contractor; the relationship is disclosed.</li>
    <li>You own the report. It's useful for budgeting, insurance files, and warranty records.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/assessment/">Learn about the assessment</a></p>
</aside>

<style>
  .assessment-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    border: 1px solid var(--cri-slate-200);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--cri-evidence);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--cri-white);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    max-width: var(--content-max);
  }
  .assessment-note__label {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    color: var(--cri-evidence);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .assessment-note h2 { font-size: var(--text-xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .assessment-note p, .assessment-note li { font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .assessment-note ul { padding-left: 1.3rem; margin-block: var(--space-3); }
  .assessment-note li + li { margin-top: var(--space-1); }
  @media print { .assessment-note { display: none; } }
</style>
